> Newbie question here, whats L and h stand for?

They're the symbols for liches and humanoids, respectively,  L includes
master liches and arch-liches, h includes mind flayers and master mind
flayers, which are generally considered to be the most deadly critters
in the game (apart from Archons and the riders, and certain
demons, which you can't genocide).  Regular liches and demiliches suck, too.  
You generally get 3 or 4 L critters on the castle level, and sometimes a 
(M)MF gets generated, although not initally.

They're sort of the standard answer to the "what should I genocide?"
question.  People also like genociding ;, R, and T, although they're
considered a lower priority, and I generally don't understand the 
rationale behind genociding T.  I much prefer to genocide U, just
because they're effing annoying, even if not deadly.

